From 918bef74073b23b1dca932c0a5acefd6f6bfebea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:16:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Origin ledger: an owner the Board removed keeps its
 verified completions settled; a re-homed card drops the old binding

Problem: 2026-11-18, after 2a234f4444d. The last stuck rows were origin-ledger obligations (`via: origin`) on
removed workers 2-8: 29 in MacBook chats, 4 in hub chats. 30 of the 33 were verified completions the ledger had
already released (`released = 1`); they still projected `unknown` and unfinished. Two hub rows were cards the
Board had re-homed from worker-3 to the hub (one done, one running).

Why 1: `project` marks a row observed only when it is `current` (the replica holds exactly its stored version) or
`settled` (current and released, 1b5a0f853f9).
Why 2: the Board drops a removed machine's records, so no row can ever be current again, and settled needs current.
Why 3: a re-home moves the card's `created_on` to the new owner; the origin ledger's binding keeps naming the old
owner, and no rule follows the move.
Root (happened): the ledger had a case for a quiet owner whose record is still published, none for an owner that
no longer exists, and none for a re-homed card.
Root (not caught): no test removed the owner from the replica after the ledger observed its completion.

Fix (`kanban_origin_ledger.project`, fresh replica only, not this gateway's own cards): an owner is removed when
the replica holds neither an info row nor a task record for it (an offline owner keeps its info row). For such a
row:
- another gateway publishing the same card (board, id, non-null created_at, `_published_elsewhere`) owns it now:
  the binding to the old owner is not projected; the new owner's record speaks for the card;
- otherwise a stored verified completion is settled (released, done), as for a quiet owner;
- an archive with owner evidence but no verified completion is closed (`closed_uncompleted`), as when observed;
- an unverified completion stays unknown, and so does an open card (its last observed status may be out of date).
`project`'s owner-scope decoding moved unchanged into `_owner_scope` (complexity cap).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_release_survives_owner_offline.py (verified completion stays released after
removal; unverified stays unknown; an owner with its info row is offline, not removed; a stale replica proves no
removal; a removed owner's open card stays unknown; a re-homed card with the same created_at drops the binding
and one with another created_at does not). 51 origin-ledger test files (935 tests) pass on the hub.
Dry run of the patched projection on the MacBook's live data: stuck rows 29 -> 0; on the hub's, 4 -> 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
